{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PHASE 1 EXIT — proven root cause (rebar-debug fast path)\n\nRuntime reproduction on scc 3.7.0 traced the actual production call in `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke`:\n\n- argv executed: `['/opt/homebrew/bin/scc', '--format', 'json', '.']`\n- parsed `Files` counts: 27 language groups, all zero\n- `_run_metric` result: `[]`, even though the repository contains files above the shipped 800-code-line cutoff\n- counterfactual with the same binary and input plus `--by-file`: 2,912 per-file entries, 29 with `Code > 800`\n\nConfirmed root cause: `_metric_invoke` omits scc's `--by-file` option at `engine_b_backends.py:376`. scc therefore emits only language summaries with empty `Files` arrays. `_scc_files` at lines 429-436 correctly consumes only per-file entries and consequently yields none; the threshold loop at lines 412-425 never executes and no metric match can be emitted. The only plausible alternative—that parsing or threshold comparison rejects otherwise-present entries—is ruled out by passing the same binary's `--by-file` JSON through `_scc_files`, which produced the expected 2,912 entries and 29 over-cutoff candidates.\n\nLegitimacy: `defect`. `src/rebar/grounding/detectors/builtin/smell_metric_oversize.yaml` authoritatively says `oversize_loc` flags files over a LOC cutoff, while `engine_b_backends.py:339-344` promises a present metric binary emits a match per file over the cutoff. Current behavior violates both contracts. Closed bug `rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab` independently established the same scc output contract for the metrics adapter and explicitly identified grounding `_scc_files` as a separate consumer.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is that a present scc invocation yields normalized matches for every returned file whose `Code` exceeds the configured cutoff, while below-cutoff files and all existing fail-open paths remain unchanged. The bounded caller sweep found `_metric_invoke` called only by `_run_metric`; that runner is dispatched through Engine B scan and then the grounding oracle. These callers consume evidence records and contractually expect matches, not an empty result. No behavioral dependency on the defect exists.\n\nFast-path criteria: deterministic reproduction, one directly observed mechanism, and a one-argument localized/reversible repair all hold. Phase 2 is unlocked after current plan review."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786913144351601001,"uuid":"5f5e4583-991c-43ee-9751-714f0ba8f162"}